-- title:
--   [HOPW18], as used in §4.5.3: polynomial invariants of a finitely generated matrix semigroup are decidable
-- statement:
--   There is an algorithm which, given $d$, finitely many $d\times d$ matrices $B_1,\dots,B_s$ and finitely many polynomials $P_1,\dots,P_t$ in the $d^2$ matrix entries, all with algebraic entries and coefficients (presented by a rational polynomial and an isolating box), decides whether
--
--   $$P_j(M)=0\quad\text{for every } M\in\langle B_1,\dots,B_s\rangle \text{ and every } j,$$
--
--   where $\langle B_1,\dots,B_s\rangle$ is the semigroup generated by the $B_i$ under matrix multiplication.
--
--   The paper (§4.5.3, p.47) reduces Item 5 of the criterion of Theorem 4.9 to such a check and cites Hrushovski, Ouaknine, Pouly and Worrell (LICS 2018) for the computability of the Zariski closure of a finitely generated matrix semigroup; the statement above is the consequence of that result used for the decidability of the dichotomy.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: "the Zariski closure of a finitely generated semigroup of matrices is computable, [so] this is decidable" → a `Computable` decider for "every matrix of the generated semigroup is a common zero of the given polynomials"; reason: the consequence of [HOPW18] used on p.47; stating the Zariski-closure computation itself would need a presentation of ideals
--   - encoding: matrices and polynomials with algebraic entries → row-major lists of `AlgPres` (rational polynomial plus isolating box); terms with exponent lists; reason: standard finite presentation; invalid presentations are excluded
-- source:
--   Cai, Ihm, Group Action and Spin Representation Lead to a Holant* Complexity Dichotomy on Domain Size 3, STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2610.04750 (held manuscript sha256 b608db44…), §4.5.3, p.47, citing [HOPW18] (Hrushovski, Ouaknine, Pouly, Worrell, Polynomial Invariants for Affine Programs, LICS 2018)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Holant3Dich_AlgPres

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Holant3Dich

/-- **[HOPW18], as used in §4.5.3: polynomial invariants of a finitely generated matrix semigroup
are decidable.** Cai–Ihm, *Group Action and Spin Representation Lead to a Holant\* Complexity
Dichotomy on Domain Size 3*, STOC 2027 submission, arXiv:2610.04750 (held manuscript sha256
b608db44…), §4.5.3, p.47: "M satisfying the tractability condition is equivalent to the Zariski
closure of M being contained in the algebraic set that corresponds to the polynomial conditions.
By [HOPW18], since the Zariski closure of a finitely generated semigroup of matrices is computable,
this is decidable." ([HOPW18]: Hrushovski, Ouaknine, Pouly, Worrell, *Polynomial Invariants for
Affine Programs*, LICS 2018.)

**Formalization Note.** The form used on p.47: one `Computable` procedure which, given `d`, a
finite list of `d × d` matrices and a finite list of polynomials in the `d²` matrix entries, all
with algebraic entries in the presentation `AlgPres`, decides whether every matrix of the
semigroup generated by the matrices is a common zero of the polynomials. Invalid inputs may
return anything. -/
theorem hopw18_semigroup_invariant :
    ∃ dec : ℕ × List MatPres × List PolyPres → Bool, Computable dec ∧
      ∀ (d : ℕ) (Ms : List MatPres) (Ps : List PolyPres),
        (∀ m ∈ Ms, m.length = d * d ∧ ∀ p ∈ m, p.Valid) → (∀ P ∈ Ps, P.Valid) →
        (dec (d, Ms, Ps) = true ↔
          ∀ M ∈ Subsemigroup.closure {N | ∃ m ∈ Ms, N = decodeMat d m},
            ∀ P ∈ Ps, P.eval M = 0) := by sorry

end Holant3Dich
